Hi all, I'm new to this list and bluetooth in general. I'm trying to
make a DUN connection using my phone.
I've installed packages found in the bluez.org site rpms for the Red Hat
and followed some tutorials.
Everything works quite fine. I connect to the device, and set up a ppp
connection.
I have one only problem. When I start the Bluetooth service
"/etc/init.d/Bluetooth start" I get this error message:
Can't open HIDP control socket: Invalid argument.
 
Can anybody help me find a solution?
I'm not sure is this, but when I connect with my phone modem, after a
little time it does not work anymore.
 
Thanks.
Regards,
Emile

